    {
        "name": "Dry Skin",
        "name_ja": "乾燥性皮膚炎",
        "symptoms": {"flaky_skin", "scratching", "dull_quills"},
        "description": "Dry Skin (xerosis) in hedgehogs is a common dermatological condition often occurring as sequel to mite/ringworm treatment (sulfur dips cause severe drying) or from environmental humidity imbalance. 15-25% prevalence in captive animals, especially post-antiparasitic therapy. Characterized by transepidermal water loss, scaling, pruritus, and quill brittleness. Usually self-limited if humidity corrected, but persistent cases develop secondary bacterial infection (10-15%). Prevention through environmental humidity control (40-60%) and skin care post-treatment is essential.",
        "description_ja": "ハリネズミの乾燥性皮膚は一般的で、特にダニ/真菌治療後の硫黄ディップが原因(極度に乾燥化)またはは環境湿度不均衡から。飼育下15-25%有病率。経表皮水分喪失・落屑・掻痒・針脆弱化。湿度是正で多くは自己限定的だが、慢性例では二次感染(10-15%)。治療後皮膚ケアと環境湿度管理(40-60%)による予防が必須。",
        "urgency": "low",
        "recommended_tests": ["physical_exam", "husbandry_review", "skin_scraping_if_pruritus_severe"],
        "causes": "MULTIFACTORIAL: (1) ENVIRONMENTAL HUMIDITY—PRIMARY: Low environmental humidity <40% (optimal 40-60% for hedgehogs—below triggers transepidermal water loss TEWL), dry bedding/substrate that absorbs moisture, inadequate water sources for humidity (no water dish that allows water evaporation for humidification), heating systems without humidification run-on during winter, poor ventilation that dries air, climate-controlled facilities (AC without humidifier), desert/arid geographic regions. (2) POST-TREATMENT XEROSIS: Sulfur dips (lime-sulfur 2-4% topical treatment for mites/ringworm cause prolonged drying of skin—sulfur is hygroscopic, absorbs skin moisture for 2-4 weeks post-treatment even after bath), topical antifungals (miconazole/clotrimazole creams cause local drying), prolonged oral antiparasitic agents (ivermectin/doxycycline dry skin via systemic effects on sebum production). (3) DIETARY DEFICIENCY: Inadequate essential fatty acids (omega-3/omega-6 ratio imbalance), low-fat diet inappropriate for hedgehogs (naturally 10-12% dietary fat needed for skin barrier), commercial insectivore diets lacking lipid variety (poor quality ω3:ω6 balance), vitamin A deficiency rare but possible (affects keratinocyte differentiation), biotin deficiency (rare, affects sebaceous gland function). (4) AGE/PHYSIOLOGICAL: Geriatric hedgehogs >4-5 years (decreased sebaceous gland activity, slower skin turnover), post-breeding stress in females (lactation increases nutrient demands including lipids). (5) SECONDARY TO SKIN DISEASE: Post-mite infestation (skin barrier damaged from scratching, weeks to months recovery), post-ringworm (some residual keratinocyte damage after antifungal cure), prior bacterial dermatitis (damage to skin barrier integrity). (6) UNDERLYING SYSTEMIC: Hyperkeratinization disorders (rare genetic predisposition), thyroid dysfunction causing dry skin (very rare in hedgehogs, hypothyroidism <1%).",
        "causes_ja": "多因子: (1) 環境湿度【主因】: <40%低湿度(ハリネズミ最適40-60%)、乾燥した床材、水皿不足、暖房冬季乾燥、AC無加湿。(2) 治療後乾燥: 硫黄ディップ(2-4週間極度乾燥継続)、局所抗真菌薬、経口駆虫薬(全身効果)。(3) 栄養欠乏: 不十分な必須脂肪酸(ω3:ω6不均衡)、低脂肪食、ビタミンA欠乏(稀)、ビオチン欠乏(稀)。(4) 年齢: 高齢>4-5年(皮脂腺活動低下)、授乳後ストレス。(5) 二次的皮膚疾患: ダニ後(掻引→皮膚バリア障害)、真菌後。(6) 全身: 角化異常(稀)、甲状腺機能(稀)。",
        "pathophysiology": "XEROSIS PROGRESSION—3 PHASES: Phase 1 (INITIAL MOISTURE LOSS 0-2 WEEKS): Environmental humidity drops below 40% or post-treatment drying begins, transepidermal water loss (TEWL) increases from normal 3-5 g/m²/hr to 8-12 g/m²/hr (2-3x normal rate), stratum corneum hydration decreases from 20-30% to <15%, early epidermal changes with cell shrinkage, minimal clinical signs (slight dullness of quills, very light flaking if observed closely). Phase 2 (ESTABLISHED XEROSIS 2-6 WEEKS): Persistent TEWL leads to progressive stratum corneum dehydration and thickness increase (hyperkeratinization compensatory response), visible scaling/flaking develops (accumulation of keratin cells without adequate moisture for cohesion), quills appear dull/brittle (reduced moisture content in keratin shaft), mild pruritus develops from inflammatory mediators (histamine, prostaglandins from epidermal stress), scratching behavior increases slightly, exfoliation of skin visible on bedding (white/gray scales), epidermal barrier function compromised (increased lipid peroxidation from desiccation, loss of natural humectant ceramides/hyaluronic acid). Phase 3 (CHRONIC XEROSIS >6 WEEKS): If humidity not corrected, chronic adaptation and secondary pathology develop—lichenification (thick, leathery skin), hyperpigmentation develops (melanin production response to irritation), continued high TEWL with heavier scaling, moderate pruritus with self-excoriation (scratching creates microtrauma), secondary bacterial colonization risk 10-15% (scratching impairs barrier integrity, normal flora overgrow or pathogenic species invade—Staphylococcus, Streptococcus, Corynebacterium), potential folliculitis at quill base if infection establishes, systemic signs if secondary infection occurs (fever, lethargy, anorexia rare but possible if severe). Post-treatment scenario: Sulfur dips cause particularly severe Phase 1-2 progression—hedgehogs may show pronounced scaling week 1-2 post-dip, which resolves gradually weeks 3-4 if humidity maintained but worsens weeks 2-4 if humidity remains low.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "乾燥性皮膚の進行: 第1段階(初期水分喪失0-2週): 湿度<40%または治療後乾燥開始、経表皮水分喪失(TEWL)正常3-5→8-12 g/m²/hr(2-3倍)、角層水分<15%低下、臨床徴候軽微(針鈍い、軽度落屑)。第2段階(確立性乾燥2-6週): 持続TEWL→角層脱水・厚化(代償的過角化)、目に見える落屑発生(ケラチン細胞蓄積)、針脆弱化、軽度掻痒(ヒスタミン・プロスタグランジン)、掻引増加→微細外傷、バリア障害(脂質過酸化・セラミド/ヒアルロン酸喪失)。第3段階(慢性乾燥>6週): 湿度未是正→苔癬化、色素沈着、中等度掻痒、二次細菌感染リスク10-15%(掻引→バリア損傷→菌叢過剰増殖)、毛嚢炎可能。",
        "treatment": "ENVIRONMENTAL MODIFICATION—PRIMARY (most effective): (1) HUMIDITY CONTROL CRITICAL: Increase environmental humidity to 40-60% optimal range (measure with digital hygrometer placed at hedgehog level): use humidifier (ultrasonic or evaporative types, run continuously winter, check water level daily to ensure consistent output), large water dish placed at room level (water evaporation contributes ~20% humidification in enclosed space), mist cage with water spray 1-2x daily (fine mist, avoid wetting hedgehog directly but wetted bedding increases ambient humidity), paper bedding/aspen that retains moisture better than cedar/pine (maintains local humidity around bedding). Monitor humidity daily—if <40% address with equipment (humidifier), if >70% reduce humidity (mold risk, ventilation improvement). (2) BATHING MODIFICATION: Eliminate frequent bathing (common cause of xerosis from soap/water stripping natural oils), limit bathing to 1-2x per year maximum if needed (dust baths for hedgehogs optional, not required), if bathing necessary use lukewarm water (18-20°C) with minimal soap (use unscented gentle baby wash only, 5-10 min soak max), follow immediately with thorough drying and emollient application (within 5 min post-bath before evaporative drying). TOPICAL SKIN CARE: (3) POST-TREATMENT XEROSIS PROTOCOL (if history of sulfur dip/antifungal): Apply emollient within 12-24 hours post-treatment and continue 2-4 weeks: plain lanolin (100% medical grade, 2-3 drops rubbed gently to affected areas q12h), OR vitamin E oil (mixed tocopherols, not tocopherol acetate which may be irritating, small amount ~2-3 drops affected areas q12h), OR unscented moisturizer cream (Cetaphil or similar, small amount to affected skin only—avoid excessive application which traps bacteria); apply after environmental humidity already optimized (emollients + high humidity = occlusion that can worsen if humidity too high). (4) SKIN-SAFE BATHING ALTERNATIVE: Oatmeal colloidal bath (if hedgehog requires cleaning without full water bath): colloidal oatmeal solution (finely ground oats suspended in warm 18-20°C water), 5-10 minute soak 1-2x monthly if needed (gentler than soap), follow with pat dry and emollient application. DIETARY INTERVENTION: (5) ESSENTIAL FATTY ACID SUPPLEMENTATION: Add ω3/ω6 sources to diet if dry skin persists despite humidity/topical care: flax seed oil 1-2 drops added to insects or food 2-3x per week (ALA omega-3 source, converts to EPA/DHA), OR salmon oil 0.5-1 drop 2-3x per week (preformed EPA/DHA more bioavailable), or other fish oil options (ensure sourced for pets, not human supplements which may contain xylitol). High-quality insectivore diet with adequate baseline lipid content (>10% fat)—verify current diet composition. Vitamin A supplementation if deficiency suspected (rare): only if recommended by veterinarian, excess vitamin A teratogenic in breeding females. (6) BIOTIN SUPPLEMENTATION if available: biotin 0.1-0.2 mg/kg once daily (supports sebaceous gland function, though biotin deficiency rare in hedgehogs), duration 4-6 weeks if tried. SYMPTOMATIC MANAGEMENT: (7) PRURITUS MANAGEMENT if significant scratching: Meloxicam 0.2-0.3 mg/kg PO q24h × 7-10 days only (short-term, NSAIDs for inflammatory component), avoid prolonged NSAID use (GI risk). Diphenhydramine 1-2 mg/kg PO q8-12h if severe pruritus (H1 blocker for histamine-driven itch), use cautiously for 3-5 days maximum (drowsiness side effect). (8) SECONDARY INFECTION TREATMENT if bacterial dermatitis develops: Topical chlorhexidine 0.5-1% applied to affected areas q12h (topical antibacterial), OR oral enrofloxacin 5-10 mg/kg PO q12h × 7-10 days if more than localized infection (systemic coverage). (9) MONITORING: Weekly assessment of skin appearance (improvement expected week 2-4 with humidity correction), recheck humidity daily if recently modified (ensure settings maintained), trim quills if severely brittle/broken (optional, not necessary but improves appearance), resolution expected 2-4 weeks with proper intervention (if longer—reconsider other diagnoses: mites, ringworm, allergic dermatitis, nutritional deficiency, hypothyroidism).",
        "treatment_ja": "環境修正【主要】: (1) 湿度制御【重大】: 40-60%に増加(デジタル湿度計設置): 加湿器連続稼働(冬季)、大きな水皿設置、霧吹き1-2回/日、紙/アスペン寝床(保湿性高い)。湿度監視日次、<40%なら加湿器, >70%なら通気改善。(2) 入浴修正: 頻繁な入浴廃止(皮脂喪失)、最大1-2回/年、必要時ぬるま湯(18-20°C)+無香性ベビーソープのみ、5-10分浸漬、直後乾燥+エモリエント塗布。局所皮膚ケア: (3) 治療後乾燥プロトコル(硫黄ディップ/抗真菌後): 12-24時間内にエモリエント塗布2-4週(無香性ランノリン2-3滴 q12h または ビタミンEオイル 2-3滴 q12h)。(4) オートミール浴(清潔化必要時): コロイドオートミール溶液(18-20°C)、5-10分浸漬1-2回/月、乾燥後エモリエント。栄養介入: (5) 必須脂肪酸補給(乾燥が湿度修正後も続く場合): フラックスシードオイル1-2滴 2-3回/週、または サーモンオイル0.5-1滴 2-3回/週。高品質インセクティボア食>10%脂肪確認。(6) ビオチン補給(利用可能なら): ビオチン0.1-0.2mg/kg 1日1回、4-6週。対症治療: (7) 掻痒管理(著しい掻引): メロキシカム0.2-0.3mg/kg q24h × 7-10日のみ(短期)、ジフェンヒドラミン1-2mg/kg q8-12h 重症時。(8) 二次感染治療: 局所クロルヘキシジン0.5-1% q12h または エンロフロキサシン5-10mg/kg q12h × 7-10日。(9) モニタリング: 週1評価(湿度是正で改善期待2-4週)、日次湿度確認、針が脆弱なら切除(任意)。",
        "prevention": "BREEDING FACILITY PREVENTION: (1) BASELINE HUMIDITY MANAGEMENT: Establish 40-60% humidity as facility standard for all enclosures (install hygrometers in each breeding room, monitor daily log), implement humidification system (centralized if possible for consistency), particularly critical during winter when heating systems dry air (common cause of seasonal dry skin outbreaks in breeding colonies). (2) POST-TREATMENT PROTOCOL: Establish SOP for post-antiparasitic/antifungal care: automatically apply emollients (lanolin or vitamin E) to all animals post-sulfur dip × 2-4 weeks, educate caretakers on proper technique (gentle application to affected skin only, avoid excessive amounts), monitor treated animals weekly for excessive dryness, defer re-treatment if xerosis develops (spacing out sulfur dips 4-6 weeks minimum if colony treatment needed). (3) DIETARY PROTOCOL: Specify high-quality insectivore diets with documented >10% fat content, provide omega-3/omega-6 supplemented insects or add fish oil to colony diet (all animals benefit, particularly breeding females which have increased lipid demands), audit diet components at acquisition and quarterly. (4) BEDDING SELECTION: Use moisture-retaining bedding (paper-based, aspen—avoid cedar/pine for toxicity reasons and also dryness), fresh bedding 1-2x week (soiled bedding traps ammonia but also moisture, balance between hygiene and humidity), avoid extremely fine dust-free beddings (ironic—while dust-free is good, some moisture retention helps local humidity). (5) ENVIRONMENTAL DESIGN: Avoid direct AC ductwork over cages (creates micro-dry zones), position humidifier output to ensure even humidity distribution, ventilation system should not over-dry (balance air exchange with humidity retention—target 6-8 air changes/hour, not excessive >12/hour which dries). (6) WATER MANAGEMENT: Provide large open water dishes in breeding facility (in addition to bottle drinkers) for evaporative humidification contribution, daily water change/refill to maintain cleanliness while supporting humidity. (7) SEASON/CLIMATE ADJUSTMENT: Increase humidification in winter (most common dry skin season in temperate climates), adjust baseline if facility in arid climate (may need 60-70% to achieve good results, risk >75% mold), monitor for seasonal patterns in colony (if dry skin outbreaks correlate with winter/AC season, adjust preventive measures pre-emptively). (8) STAFF EDUCATION: Training on xerosis recognition (appearance of scales, dull quills, quill brittleness), understanding humidity importance (many caretakers underestimate—educational emphasis needed), proper emollient application if treatment needed (gentle, affected areas only, avoid overuse), recognition of secondary infection signs (scratching lesions, behavior change). (9) GENETIC SELECTION: No specific genetic testing available, but note families with predisposition to dry skin (some colony lines may have naturally drier skin phenotype—manage with enhanced humidification/supplementation if observed).",
        "prevention_ja": "繁殖施設予防: (1) 基礎湿度管理: 40-60%を施設標準に(各ケージに湿度計、日次監視), 加湿システム導入(冬季に特に重要), 暖房シーズン対策。(2) 治療後プロトコル: 硫黄ディップ後自動エモリエント塗布 × 2-4週、教育実施、週1監視、脱水時は治療延期(最小4-6週間間隔)。(3) 食事プロトコル: >10%脂肪食指定、ω3/ω6補給(虫または食事への添加)、四半期毎監査。(4) 寝床選択: 保湿性高い(紙/アスペン、スギ/マツ避ける), 新鮮1-2回/週。(5) 環境設計: AC直風回避, 加湿器均等配置, 換気6-8回/時(過剰避ける)。(6) 水管理: 大きな水皿設置(蒸発加湿)。(7) 季節調整: 冬季増加加湿, 乾燥気候は60-70%に上昇(>75%カビリスク)。(8) 職員教育: 乾燥症認識・湿度重要性, エモリエント塗布正確実施。(9) 遺伝的選択: 乾燥肌系統は強化加湿/補給。",
        "prognosis": "TIME-DEPENDENT PROGNOSIS: EXCELLENT 95-100% (<1 week intervention, humidity corrected to 40-60%, mild scaling only, no scratching lesions, rapid improvement expected within 3-5 days, complete resolution 1-2 weeks, no secondary infection). GOOD 85-95% (1-2 weeks intervention, moderate scaling with minor scratching lesions, humidity corrected + emollient therapy started, improvement visible week 1-2, resolution 2-3 weeks, minimal residual changes). FAIR 70-85% (>2 weeks before intervention, significant scaling/flaking, minor secondary excoriation, possible mild bacterial colonization, humidity + topical care + oral supplements, slower improvement week 2-4, extended resolution 3-4 weeks, potential residual quill brittleness). GUARDED 50-70% (chronic xerosis >4 weeks, heavy scaling with marked scratching lesions, secondary bacterial dermatitis evident, delayed intervention, slow response to therapy week 3-4, prolonged recovery 4-6+ weeks, persistent residual scaling possible). POOR <50% (extreme chronic xerosis with severe secondary infection, immunocompromised host, poor compliance with humidity maintenance, minimal improvement despite intervention, chronic management required). AGE EFFECTS: Young/adult: excellent response to humidity correction (days to weeks); geriatric >4 years: slower response (decreased sebaceous gland compensation), may require longer supplementation. COMORBIDITY: Post-mite infestation: sometimes slower healing (underlying skin barrier compromise), but usually improves with humidity once mite infection resolved; post-sulfur dip: typically excellent response if humidity optimized (week 2-3 complete). TIMELINE: Most dry skin resolves completely within 2-4 weeks of proper humidity control (40-60%) + topical care if needed. If NOT improving by week 4, reconsider diagnosis (undiagnosed mites, ringworm, allergic dermatitis, systemic disease). Post-treatment residual drying (after sulfur dip) typically resolves completely by week 4-6 with emollient use. Risk of recurrence if humidity allowed to drop again—lifetime susceptibility if predisposed.",
        "prognosis_ja": "時間依存的予後: 優(95-100%, <1週間介入, 湿度40-60%是正, 軽度落屑のみ, 掻引なし, 3-5日改善, 1-2週治癒); 良(85-95%, 1-2週, 中等度落屑+軽微掻引, 湿度+エモリエント, 2-3週治癒); 可(70-85%, >2週遅延, 著しい落屑, 軽微掻引傷, 軽度細菌定着, 3-4週治癒); 不可(50-70%, 慢性>4週, 重度掻引, 二次細菌, 遅延介入, 4-6+週); 極悪(<50%, 極度慢性+重症感染)。年齢: 若/成体は優(日-週), 高齢>4年は遅い。合併症: ダニ後: 時に遅い(バリア障害)だが解決後改善; 硫黄後: 優(2-3週)。タイムライン: ほとんどは湿度40-60%で2-4週治癒。4週で改善なし→診断再考(未検出ダニ/真菌/アレルギー)。治療後残存乾燥は4-6週で完全治癒(エモリエント使用時)。湿度低下なら再発リスク。",
        "onset_pattern": {"acute", "subacute", "chronic"},
        "age_predisposition": {"young", "adult", "senior"},
    },
